<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"/>
  <title>Where Did I Put It?</title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/>
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
  <meta name="application-name" content="WDIPI"/>
  <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
  <meta name="description" content="Here you can store and recollect information about location of your items"/>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon-96x96.png" sizes="96x96" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <link rel="shortcut icon" href="favicon.ico" />
  <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="apple-touch-icon.png" />
  <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="WDIPI" />
  <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css" />
  <script type="module" src="/js/widget.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1>Where Did I Put It?</h1>
</header>
<main>
  <section>
    <header>
      <h2>Items and places</h2>
    </header>
    <p>
      Put&nbsp;something into&nbsp;a&nbsp;"reliable place" and&nbsp;forgot where
      to&nbsp;again?<br/>
      Not&nbsp;anymore. Use this simple widget when you put&nbsp;something
      somewhere to&nbsp;memorize and&nbsp;recollect its&nbsp;location.
    </p>

    <div class="widget">
      <label>
        <span>Item</span>
        <input autocomplete="off" name="item" list="items" placeholder="Item"/>
      </label>
      <label>
        <span>Place</span>
        <input name="place" placeholder="Place"/>
      </label>
      <button type="button" class="apply">Apply</button>
    </div>

    <datalist id="items"></datalist>

    <h3>Memorizing items</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Fill in "item" field.</li>
      <li>Fill in "place" field.</li>
      <li>Press "Apply" button.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      All items are stored locally in your device using local storage. All saved
      items are added to list so you can select them later (drop-down
      for "item" field).
    </p>

    <h3>Recollecting places</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Select item from drop-down list in "item" field.</li>
      <li>Saved place should appear in "place" field.</li>
      <li>Edit "place" field and press "apply" if you need to change place for that item.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Removing items from list</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Select item from drop-down list in "item" field.</li>
      <li>Leave "place" field blank.</li>
      <li>Press "Apply" button.</li>
    </ol>

    <p><a href="list.html">Full list of items</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>About</h2>

    <p>
      I created this project because I kept forgetting where I put different
      items that I can need in distant future. Even when one says "remember:
      I put this over there", when time passes, it can be hard to recollect
      where exactly "over there" is.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wouldn't it be nice to have a lightweight tool that server the only purpose:
      memorizing and recollecting for you what you put and where? Now such tool
      exists (it may or may not have existed previously, I didn't check).
    </p>
    <p>
      You can send it to home screen of your device to have quick access when
      you need it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>

    <p>
      This site is provided "as is" without any explicit or implicit
      warranty that information is saved and can be received in the future.
    </p>
    <p>
      It uses localStorage feature of browsers to store the list of items
      locally on your device and, as a result, any third party component
      is subject to change without any notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      Make sure that you have another copy of your item/location mapping
      elsewhere if it is really critical for you to recollect the locations.
      Better safe than sorry.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      This site does not use any cookies or other technology to track you.
      The only thing used is localStorage that keeps list of item/location
      mapping. This list is not sent anywhere and is stored only on your device.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>
